WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.210
- [Instructor] We're told that Ben's home

00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:05.540
is x kilometers from an ice cream shop.

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:10.230
Jerry's home is y kilometers
from the same shop.

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:12.900
Then it tells us they each left
their home at the same time

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:16.700
and met at the ice cream
shop at the same time.

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:20.460
Ben walked an average speed,
let me do this in a new color,

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:23.040
average speed of five kilometers per hour.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:27.110
And Jerry rode his bicycle
at an average speed

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:29.220
of v kilometers per hour.

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:32.310
Write an equation that
relates x, y, and v.

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:34.443
Pause this video and
see if you can do that.

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:38.240
All right, so let's just remind ourselves

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:41.760
how distance, speed, and time are related.

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:43.770
You might be familiar with things like

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:46.630
distance is equal to rate times time,

00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:47.990
or another way you could think about it is

00:00:47.990 --> 00:00:49.390
you could write the distance

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:55.183
is equal to speed times time.

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.650
Or if you wanna solve for time,

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:00.960
you can divide both sides by speed.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:05.640
So you could get distance over speed,

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:09.133
over speed, is equal to time.

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:11.970
Now the reason why I set it up this way

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:13.970
is that we know that Ben's time

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:16.000
and Jerry's time is the same.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.480
They covered maybe different distances

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:21.380
at maybe different
speeds, but it took them

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:23.890
the exact same amount of time.

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:26.670
So Ben's distance divided by Ben's speed

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:29.060
should be the same as Jerry's distance

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:30.640
divided by Jerry's speed.

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:32.290
So let me write that down.

00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:36.903
So Ben's distance, Ben's distance,

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:41.483
divided by Ben's speed,

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:44.070
and let me write it in this color,

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:49.843
Ben's speed should be equal to

00:01:51.910 --> 00:01:56.023
Jerry's distance, Jerry's distance,

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:01.883
divided by Jerry's speed,

00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:06.663
Jerry's speed.

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:09.490
Now which of these do we know

00:02:09.490 --> 00:02:11.560
or do we already have variables to find?

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:13.910
Well we know that Ben's
distance from the ice cream shop

00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:16.740
is x, so this is represented by x.

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:18.910
We know that Jerry's distance
from the ice cream shop

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:21.770
is represented by y, so this is y.

00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:25.940
we know that Ben's speed is
five kilometers per hour.

00:02:25.940 --> 00:02:28.030
So we're assuming everything
is in kilometers per hour.

00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:29.890
So this would be five.

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:33.560
And then Jerry's speed
is v kilometers per hour.

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:36.490
So this is v right over there.

00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:39.430
And so we could rewrite all of this as

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:41.400
x over five

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:47.390
is equal to y over v.

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:50.730
And once again, the
way that I set this up,

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:53.150
the left side is the
amount of time Ben takes

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:54.570
to get to the ice cream shop.

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:56.180
This is, on the right hand side,

00:02:56.180 --> 00:02:57.430
this is the amount of time Jerry takes

00:02:57.430 --> 00:02:58.970
to get to the ice cream shop.

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:01.830
And they tell us it's
the same amount of time.

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:02.663
So there you have it.

00:03:02.663 --> 00:03:05.400
We have an equation that
relates x, y, and v.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:07.240
And they gave us the five.

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:09.820
Now it's completely possible
that instead of the five,

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:10.990
they gave us something else

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:12.780
and Ben's speed was the variable.

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:15.260
If they did that, then we
would have a different given

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:16.320
and maybe a different variable,

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:19.380
but the structure of our
equation would be the same,

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:22.040
that Ben's distance divided by Ben speed's

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:24.540
would need to be equal to Jerry's distance

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:26.283
divided by Jerry's speed.

